[[File:Gardener Asgore (Beta 41.1).png|thumb|182x182px|Beta 41.1]]
Gardener Asgore was added in '''Beta 30.0''' with the Magic ability to remove negative effects from ally monsters, which he (fittingly) shares with [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Asriel Asriel], alongside the same stats of 4/4 for 5G and [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Epic Epic] Rarity. However, this was limited to [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Plant Plants]. To compensate, he also added 2 random Plants to your hand. This last part was nerfed in '''Beta 41.1''', as this was now limited to just the 2 [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Generate Generated] Plants: [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Flower_Jar Red Flower] and [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Flower_Can Green Flower], of which he gives one of each.
[[File:Gardener Asgore (Beta 48.0).png|thumb|179x179px|Beta 48.0]]
'''Beta 48.0''' heavily reworked it. Now, he's a 3/5 for 7G with a Turn end effect of turning a random ally Green Flower into a Red Flower (effectively giving it +4/+4). If there's no Red, he will simply summon a Green instead. '''Beta 50.1''' reworked Red Flower. As a result, this was changed (but buffed) to make [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Blue_Flower Blue Flower] the result from the transformation (which, compared to the old Red Flower, has the same ATK and HP, but -2G and Taunt).
[[File:Gardener Asgore (Beta 50.1).png|thumb|177x177px|Beta 50.1]]
'''Beta 52.1''' changed him once more (after Blue Flower's cost increased by 2G). His Turn end effect was changed into a Delay effect, making it only trigger once (and he has to be actually played). To compensate, he gained +1 HP and if there is no Green Flower on your board, he will now summon a Red Flower (effectively giving it +2/+2 and Transparency).

=== Stats ===
ATK:
* 4 (Post Beta 30.0)
* 3 (Post Beta 48.0, Current)
HP:
* 4 (Post Beta 30.0)
* 5 (Post Beta 48.0)
* 6 (Post Beta 52.1, Current)
Cost:
* 5 (Post Beta 30.0)
* 7 (Post Beta 48.0, Current)
Abilities:
* Magic: Remove all negative effects from all ally Plants.
** Add 2 random Plants to your hand. (Post Beta 30.0)
** Add a Green Flower and Red Flower to your hand. (Post Beta 41.1)
* Turn end: If there is no ally Green Flower, summon one. If there is, ...
** turn a random ally Green Flower into a Red Flower. (Post Beta 48.0)
** turn a random ally Green Flower into a Blue Flower. (Post Beta 50.1)
* Delay: If there is no ally Green Flower, summon a Red Flower. If there is, ...
** turn a random ally Green Flower into a Blue Flower. (Post Beta 52.1, Current)
Rarity: Purple (Epic)
